op in diocesesBishop in every civitas. Bishop\'s church called ecclesia, other churches were basilicae. City had complex of religious buildings, usually included a number of churches, a baptistery, and the bishop\'s home (domus ecclesiae). Other religious officials were the clergy. Outside the city were funerary basilicas, sacred sites (shrines called loca sancta), mausoleums, tombs and cemeteries. Authorities secular and often came into conflict with religious authorities. <br>Dioceses provided basic structure of Merovingian Church, "the ecclesiastical counterparts of the civitates" and in the same place, except in the north and east. <br>3. Subordinate bishopsDioceses had provinces (like civitates) <br>4. Priests5. Lesser clergy<br>'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1020, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 875})
